   "evidence": "engine.ts:2776-2786 at head: `await pushBranch(..., head, ctx.signal, budget, ctx.state.publishedSha ?? null); ctx.state.publishedSha = head; await ctx.save(\"delivery-pushed\");`. Nothing is saved before the push, so a crash between the push and the save leaves publishedSha unset while the remote holds H1. On resume, `deliver` calls `fetchBase`. If the base advanced, `mergeForDelivery` produces H2, and pushBranch with `expected=null` uses `--force-with-lease=refs/heads/<b>:`, which is refused because the branch exists. The fallback `remoteBranchSha(...) !== head` (repos.ts:1571-1573) only accepts a remote that already equals H2, so the push throws. At base, the bare `--force-with-lease` to a URL behaves the same way (it also expects the branch to be absent), so the PR does not make this worse; the reviewer says the same. The request requires saving after the push, not reconciling before it."
